  "response": "**Calculation (Bayes' theorem):**\n\n- Prevalence: P(D) = 1/500 = 0.002, so P(¬D) = 0.998\n- Sensitivity: P(+|D) = 0.98\n- Specificity: P(−|¬D) = 0.95 → P(+|¬D) = 0.05\n\nP(+) = P(+|D)·P(D) + P(+|¬D)·P(¬D)\n = (0.98 × 0.002) + (0.05 × 0.998)\n = 0.00196 + 0.0499\n = 0.05186\n\nP(D|+) = P(+|D)·P(D) / P(+) = 0.00196 / 0.05186 ≈ 0.037794\n\nConverting to a percentage: **≈ 3.78%**\n\nEven with a fairly accurate test, because the condition is rare, most positive results are false positives — only about 1 in 26 people who test positive actually have the condition.\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 3.78",
